================================================================================
WHERE THE HOST CAN STILL EDIT THE SPEC, and what Docker's --gpus puts in it.
containerd 1.7.27, Docker 28.1.1, 2026-08-28.
================================================================================

--- 1. containerd writes config.json BEFORE it exec's the shim binary ------
The shim wrapper was replaced with one that logs its argv, its cwd and the
directory listing, then exec'd the real Kata shim.

=== 2026-08-28T02:32:18 argv: /usr/local/bin/containerd-shim-nvkvm-kata-v2
      -namespace moby -address /run/containerd/containerd.sock
      -publish-binary /usr/bin/containerd -id 6aac9919ad07... start
cwd: /run/containerd/io.containerd.runtime.v2.task/moby/6aac9919ad07...
total 12
drwx------ 3 root root   120 Aug 28 02:32 .
-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 10159 Aug 28 02:32 config.json      <-- present
prwx------ 1 root root     0 Aug 28 02:32 log
drwx--x--x 2 root root    40 Aug 28 02:32 rootfs
CONFIG PRESENT 10159

=== 2026-08-28T02:32:19 argv: ... -bundle ... delete
CONFIG PRESENT 10159

So `start` runs with the bundle as the working directory and the OCI spec
already written.  That is the last point on the host at which the spec can be
edited, and it needs no Kata change to reach.

--- 2. what `docker run --runtime=nvkvm-kata --gpus all` produces ----------
(from that same config.json)

ENV:
    PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    HOSTNAME=6aac9919ad07
    NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=all                 <-- the whole request, as data
HOOKS: {
 "prestart": [
  { "path": "/usr/bin/nvidia-container-runtime-hook",
    "args": ["nvidia-container-runtime-hook", "prestart"], ... } ] }
MOUNTS: 10
DEVICES: None
RESDEV: [{'allow': False, 'access': 'rwm'}, ... no NVIDIA entries ...]

Docker sets the environment variable and adds the toolkit's legacy prestart
hook.  It injects no mounts, no device nodes and no cgroup rules -- those are
the hook's job.

--- 3. and that hook does not survive Kata --------------------------------
$ docker run --runtime=nvkvm-kata --gpus all --rm ubuntu:24.04 /bin/true
docker: Error response from daemon: failed to create task for container:
failed to create shim task: exit status 1: stdout: , stderr:
Auto-detected mode as 'legacy'
nvidia-container-cli: mount error: mount operation failed:
/var/lib/docker/overlay2/0786abb7.../merged/proc/driver/nvidia:
no such file or directory
docker rc=127

journalctl -t kata:
  level=error msg="hook error" ... hook-type=pre-start subsystem=hook
  level=error msg="fail to run prestartHook for sandbox 6aac9919ad07..."

Kata DOES run host prestart hooks (src/runtime/pkg/katautils/create.go:194),
on the host, where the container rootfs is an overlay directory the guest will
later see over virtio-fs -- so the hook's bind mounts would not traverse and
its device nodes would carry host major/minor.  This is the field failure
reported in kata#10672.

CONSEQUENCE: before this change, `docker run --runtime=nvkvm-kata --gpus all`
did not merely fail to get a GPU, it FAILED TO START.  The injector removes the
hook and does the four things it would have done, in the places that work.
